    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d815">

                <pb facs="0853" n="803" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg803"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Dr. Lobo to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Venezuela</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-26"><hi rendition="#italic">October 26,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Dr. David Lobo, chargé d’affaires <hi rendition="#italic">ad interim</hi> of
                    Venezuela, presents his compliments to the Secretary of State, and in compliance
                    with the request expressed by the Secretary at the interview of October 24 has
                    the honor to inclose herewith a brief review of the boundary question pending
                    between Venezuela and Great Britain.</p>
                <p>He asks the Secretary also to inform him on what day it will be convenient to the
                    former to have him call at the Department for a fresh discussion of the subject
                    referred to.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
